A log kept 100 years in ~347,000 partitions, with SHARDS 64: each shard gets ~0.0029
events/s, so batches average 1.0014 events. An entity's events come through 64
change-stream shards, so its row in user_totals holds 64 high-water marks: 87 B + 64 × 29.7
B = 1.94 KB, or 2 write units. Under SPLIT 3 an item holds ~21 marks (0.70 KB, 1 write
unit; SPLIT 2 leaves 1.01 KB), which halves the row writes: 2,200 write and 1,100 read
units/s cost $3,975 a month, and 1,100 of each cost $2,168, saving $1,807.
-- dynaflux.yaml --
store: analytics
regions: [us-east-1]
-- dynaflux/page_views.sql --
CREATE STREAM page_views (user_id String, page String, duration_ms UInt32)
PRIMARY KEY (user_id)
SHARDS 64
LOG RETENTION 36525 DAY;
-- dynaflux/views.sql --
CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW user_totals
ORDER BY (user_id)
AS SELECT user_id, count() AS views, sum(duration_ms) AS total_ms
FROM page_views
GROUP BY user_id;
-- explain page_views --
stream page_views
  assumptions  --rate 1000  --event-kb 1
               (traffic isn't in the SQL or dynaflux.yaml; set it with these flags)
  prices       us-east-1 list prices, ±30%: for comparing designs, not a quote

layout, in us-east-1
  table        analytics-stream-page_views: Global Table, on-demand
  key          pk user_id and a shard of 64; sk event_time, event_id
  log          LOG RETENTION 36525 DAY: ~3,471,336 GB in ~347,134 partitions, each a change-stream shard
  projector    batching window 1 s, batches of at most 100 events: ~999 invocations/s, 1 event each on average
  marks        a view row keeps a shard's high-water mark for 960 s after the shard's progress passes it (runtime.prune_window_seconds)
  archive      Firehose to Iceberg in us-east-1

per event, per region             write units  read units
  event put, local or replicated         1.00
  user_totals, a row per entity          2.20        1.10
  progress item, one per batch           1.00
  total                                  4.20        1.10
  per second, all events                4,199       1,100

monthly                        per region  1 region
  DynamoDB requests                $7,257    $7,257
    stream and meta tables         $3,283    $3,283
    user_totals                    $3,975    $3,975
  DynamoDB storage of the log    $867,834  $867,834
  Lambda, the projector            $1,645    $1,645
  Firehose                           $142      $142
  S3 archive, year-1 average          $73       $73
  replication transfer              $0.00     $0.00
  total                          $876,951  $876,951
  provisioned capacity at a 70% target would cut requests to $2,995 per region (-59%), but costs more than on-demand if it must cover peaks over 2.42 times the average
  not modeled: query reads, view and marker storage, backfills, archive compaction, CloudWatch

warning page_views: batches average 1 event over 347,134 shards, so view writes rarely combine: most events cost a row write in every view
  hint: shorten LOG RETENTION, which means fewer shards, or raise runtime.batching_window_seconds
warning page_views: ~347,134 shards per region: after an outage, the projector catches up with one invocation per shard, over Lambda's default quota of 1,000 concurrent executions, which all of the account's functions in a region share
  hint: shorten LOG RETENTION, or raise the account's Lambda concurrency quota
warning user_totals: rows reach 1.62 KB with ~64 high-water marks, one for each change-stream shard that SHARDS 64 spreads an entity's events over; every write costs 2 write units
  hint: SPLIT 2 keeps each item at 1 write unit, saving ~$1,807 a month per region; queries then read 2 items per row; or use fewer SHARDS on page_views
-- explain user_totals --
view user_totals, from stream page_views
  assumptions  --rate 1000  --event-kb 1
               (traffic isn't in the SQL or dynaflux.yaml; set it with these flags)
  prices       us-east-1 list prices, ±30%: for comparing designs, not a quote

layout, in us-east-1
  table        analytics-view-user_totals-v1: regional, on-demand
  mode         ASYNC: the projector applies events in batches
  rows         a row per entity: GROUP BY (user_id) holds user_id, the PRIMARY KEY of page_views
  backfill     fenced handoff: count and sum are additive

row, estimated (String values are taken as 32 bytes)
  pk        user_id                                                  34 B
  sk        a constant                                                3 B
  user_id   key column                                               39 B
  views     count()                                                  13 B
  total_ms  sum(duration_ms)                                         20 B
  _v        row version                                              10 B
  _hwm      ~64 high-water marks of ~24 B                         1.51 KB
  total     2 write units, 1 read unit; the item limit is 400 KB  1.62 KB

per event, per region
  rows         2.20 write units and 1.10 read units: a batch of 1 event updates 1 row, and 10% of writes conflict and retry
  monthly      DynamoDB requests $3,975 per region, $3,975 for 1 region

warning user_totals: rows reach 1.62 KB with ~64 high-water marks, one for each change-stream shard that SHARDS 64 spreads an entity's events over; every write costs 2 write units
  hint: SPLIT 2 keeps each item at 1 write unit, saving ~$1,807 a month per region; queries then read 2 items per row; or use fewer SHARDS on page_views
